<pre class=metadata>
Title: Privacy Protections for Media Features
Shortname: media-feature-privacy
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/CSS-Additions/system-media-queries/privacy-protections/spec/
Repository: arronei/CSS-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: Media features that describe the user's system, such as whether power saving is on or which
    accessibility settings are turned on, can be read by style sheets as well as by script, and a style
    sheet can report what it reads to a server without running any script. This specification defines
    the protections that the system media query specifications apply to such features:
    [=protected evaluation=], which lets a page change its appearance without learning the value;
    [=delayed change delivery=], which stops a change from linking the user's visits to different sites;
    [=frame-scoped exposure=], which limits what embedded third-party content learns; and
    [=reduced-exposure contexts=], in which features report fixed values. It also defines the threat
    model and the way of measuring fingerprinting that those specifications share.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css yes
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

